    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. I'm Dr. Smith. To get us started, could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Hi, Dr. Smith. Um, well, I guess what really made me come in is... I just can't shake this feeling lately. Like, at work, I do the buying for this retail chain, mostly electronics and seasonal stuff, and I swear people there, and even some of the vendors we use, they're tracking my buys. Like, specifically watching what I do and messing with the launch numbers just to make me look stupid. Which is crazy because I used to love talking to the vendors. I actually met this one guy from a headphone company last year, and he had this insane collection of vintage walkmans. We talked for like an hour about cassette tapes, which my dad used to collect too. He had this whole basement full of them, mostly classic rock, and he'd always get mad if I touched them... but anyway, yeah, my supervisor keeps showing me these reports trying to prove that nobody's messing with my numbers, but I just know they are. I can feel it.",
