    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During these past ten months, have there been any periods where your mood felt significantly different, such as feeling extremely low, hopeless, or unusually energetic and elated?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, actually, there are times where I feel totally different. Like, I'll get these stretches where I feel like the whole city is just opening up for me, you know? Like I'm completely dialed in and I have all this energy. I'll be walking downtown and the architecture just looks so sharp, like the old brick buildings against the glass ones. Have you ever noticed how they mix the zoning downtown? I was reading about city planning the other night, and they used to just build factories right next to houses in the 1800s. There's this one building near my apartment that used to make umbrellas, of all things. I don't know who buys umbrellas anymore, they always break in the wind. My mom bought me one of those fancy windproof ones once, but I left it on the subway. The subway is crazy late at night, by the way... but anyway, yeah, I'll feel amazing, but then if someone at work questions a purchase order or tells me I need to slow down, I just snap. Like, way harder than I mean to. I get so irritable and angry so fast when I'm in that zone.",
